course: dictionary
lesson: 7432
title: Pollinate: how flowers make seeds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To pollinate a flower means to carry pollen from one flower to another, so seeds can form. Pollen comes from the male part of a flower, the stamen, and it must reach the female part, the stigma. «Bees pollinate flowers (carry pollen from flower to flower so seeds and fruit can grow).»
explain: Look at the clues in that sentence: carry pollen, and so seeds and fruit can grow. Pollinate is the job, and seeds are the result. Try the check: swap in "carry pollen from flower to flower" and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Animals are not the only pollinators, because the wind can do the job too. «Bees pollinate many fruit crops, such as apples and strawberries.» Grasses and birch trees are pollinated by the wind instead. Notice the different forms: pollinate, pollinates, pollinated, pollinating.
fact: Pollinate is a verb: I pollinate, it pollinates, they pollinated, it is pollinating.
fact: Pollen moves from the stamen (male part) to the stigma (female part) of a flower.
fact: «Insect-pollinated» flowers are pollinated by insects such as bees, butterflies and moths, which drink nectar as they go.
fact: «Wind-pollinated» plants, such as grasses, make huge amounts of light pollen that the wind carries.
fact: Without pollination, many fruits and crops would not grow, so protecting bees matters.
exercise: «Bees pollinate many fruit crops, such as apples and strawberries.» What does pollinate mean? | Eat the fruit from the tree | Water the plants in the sun | *Carry pollen from flower to flower so seeds can form | Pick the flowers to sell them
exercise: Grasses and birch trees are «wind-pollinated». What does that tell you? | Birds fly to them to drink nectar | *The wind carries their pollen | They are only grown indoors | Insects are needed to carry their pollen
exercise: Which of these is an insect that can pollinate flowers while it drinks nectar? | Trees | Rabbit | Stone | *Butterfly
test: Which part of a flower receives pollen? | Stamen | Leaf | Petal | *Stigma
test: «Without pollination, many fruits and crops would not grow.» What does this suggest? | Bees are not important | Crops only need sunshine | *Pollination helps fruit and crops to grow | Fruit grows without any help at all
exam: Which sentence uses pollinate correctly? | Sleep pollinates the children. | The fish pollinated the pond. | *Birds and bats sometimes pollinate flowers. | The car pollinates the road.
